### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 10 — MEMORY, COMPACTION & LONG-TERM CONTEXT SEARCH
###
### ArcClaw uses a dual-SQLite memory system:
###
###   arcclaw-meta.db (primary WAL)
###     └─ chat_memory            — rolling LangChain4J chat window (max 20 msgs)
###     └─ compaction_summary     — summary records from compaction runs
###     └─ agent_checkpoint       — per-session ReAct state
###
###   arcclaw-fts.db (FTS5)
###     └─ compaction_summary_fts — full-text indexed summaries, queryable via
###                                 MemorySearchTool
###
### Compaction trigger:
###   When chat window exceeds: max-messages (20) - keep-recent (5) = threshold (5+)
###   → ContextCompactionService summarises the oldest messages
###   → Compact summary stored in both meta.db and fts.db
###   → Most recent 5 messages kept verbatim
###   → Model used for compaction: llama-3.1-8b-instant (cheap, fast)
###   → Audit event written: CONTEXT_COMPACTED
###
### MemorySearchTool (memory_search):
###   Queries FTS5 using userId scope — tenant-isolated.
###   Available to: coordinator, researcher, architect, synthesizer.
###   Input: {query: "<search terms>"}
###   Returns: top-N matching compaction summaries
###
### Conversation continuity:
###   Chat memory (ChatMemoryStore) is NOT wiped on session soft-reset.
###   Only the ReAct checkpoint state is cleared.
###   → LLM retains conversational context across multiple goals.
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw serve mode, GROQ_API_KEY set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = Fxa8CCQGpjHr7DS3eiSTlb3W0RKzImwHXPkNbq9S98c=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MULTI-TURN CONVERSATION
# The rolling chat memory makes the agent aware of prior exchanges
# within the same session. This tests conversational continuity.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [MEM-0] Create session for multi-turn test
# @name memSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MEM-1] First message — establish a fact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Remember this: my project is called ArcClaw and it uses Quarkus 3.23.0.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [MEM-2] Second message — recall from chat memory (no tools)
# The LLM sees prior turn in its rolling window, should recall correctly
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What was the project name I told you about, and which framework does it use?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [MEM-3] Third turn — build on the context further
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Given what you know about my project, what JVM version does Quarkus 3.23.0 require?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROLLING WINDOW PRUNING
# Chat window is capped at 20 messages (configurable).
# After 20+ messages, older ones are pruned from the window.
# Watch logs for: [MemoryPruning] pruned N messages session=...
#
# Send 22 sequential messages to see the window prune the oldest 2.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [MEM-4] Create a dedicated session for window pruning test
# @name pruneSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### Msg 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{pruneSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{"goal": "Memory window test message 1: What is virtual threading?", "agentRole": "coordinator", "maxIterations": 1}


###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{pruneSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### Msg 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{pruneSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{"goal": "Memory window test message 2: What is SQLite WAL mode?", "agentRole": "coordinator", "maxIterations": 1}

###

### Msg 3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{pruneSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{"goal": "Memory window test message 3: What is Podman?", "agentRole": "coordinator", "maxIterations": 1}

###

